        "workflow": {
          "name": "archon-intake",
          "description": "The standing front of the label-driven pack. Every issue event records a\nrequest on the issue's work item; the run then claims the best waiting item\nand decides, with a script and before any model reads the text, whether its\nauthor is a listed maintainer. A maintainer's issue is triaged, and the\nverdict becomes the item's stage and a route label; a duplicate or an\nalready delivered item the triage policy lets close is closed with a link to\nwhat resolved it. An outside issue gets\narchon-needs-maintainer and starts no agent until a listed maintainer\npromotes it by adding archon-triage or a route label. With mode eval the run\nwrites nothing: it decides the named issue as it was opened and returns the\nwhole decision as its output.\n\nUse when: trigger bindings start it on issue lifecycle and label events (see\nthe SDLC pack README, \"Intake\").\nNOT for: triaging one item by hand (archon-triage), or delivering work.\n",
